WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:05.843
This is a technical walkthrough of Relay version one point one: how it is built,

2
00:00:05.843 --> 00:00:09.865
why the model reasons but the backend decides, and how it was tested.

3
00:00:11.565 --> 00:00:15.862
Relay is a Wasp application: React and TypeScript in the browser,

4
00:00:15.862 --> 00:00:18.969
Node on the server, and Prisma over PostgreSQL.

5
00:00:18.969 --> 00:00:24.192
Every action is a server operation that checks who you are and what you may do,

6
00:00:24.192 --> 00:00:26.505
then hands over to the case engine.

7
00:00:26.505 --> 00:00:31.728
Background work runs as pg-boss jobs inside the same Postgres: the coordinator,

8
00:00:31.728 --> 00:00:36.091
chat replies, vendor discovery, and a deadline sweep every minute.

9
00:00:36.091 --> 00:00:40.586
The model is any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, here a small local one.

10
00:00:40.586 --> 00:00:45.875
Fiber AI, email, voice and tracing are optional, and the app works without them.

11
00:00:47.575 --> 00:00:49.613
Every write follows one pattern.

12
00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:54.136
Lock the case row, check the transition against a shared state machine,

13
00:00:54.136 --> 00:00:58.595
and write the change, its event and any follow-ups in one transaction.

14
00:00:58.595 --> 00:01:01.334
Each status has an owner and a next action.

15
00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:06.685
Idempotency keys and partial unique indexes make retries and double clicks harmless.

16
00:01:08.385 --> 00:01:10.182
The agents are event driven.

17
00:01:10.182 --> 00:01:15.574
When a transition matters, the same transaction writes a durable marker on the case,

18
00:01:15.574 --> 00:01:17.949
and after the commit a job is queued.

19
00:01:17.949 --> 00:01:22.570
The job claims that exact trigger once, runs a deterministic step first,

20
00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:26.614
then a bounded tool loop with the model, and clears the marker.

21
00:01:26.614 --> 00:01:28.411
Nothing runs between events.

22
00:01:28.411 --> 00:01:33.032
If a job is lost, the minute sweep finds the marker and queues it again.

23
00:01:33.032 --> 00:01:36.755
If a review fails, it is recorded and the manager is told.

24
00:01:38.455 --> 00:01:40.435
The model reads and proposes.

25
00:01:40.435 --> 00:01:41.323
Code decides.

26
00:01:41.323 --> 00:01:45.625
Offers go only to vendors in the property's approved directory.

27
00:01:45.625 --> 00:01:49.995
Messages to residents must pass a grounding check and a manager.

28
00:01:49.995 --> 00:01:54.911
An escalation runs at once only if the deterministic safety rules agree.

29
00:01:54.911 --> 00:02:00.715
And no tool can approve money, schedule a visit, close a case, or contact a business.

30
00:02:02.415 --> 00:02:08.150
When a property has no approved vendor for a trade, the coordinator opens a discovery task.

31
00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:14.011
It sends Fiber only the trade and the city, checks the balance, a reserve and a daily budget,

32
00:02:14.011 --> 00:02:21.825
saves the paid response before processing, and keeps at most three businesses, each with reasons that cite only its listing.

33
00:02:21.825 --> 00:02:25.670
A manager must verify and approve a business before any work.

34
00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.371
No Fiber key was available,

35
00:02:27.371 --> 00:02:33.295
so no live call was made: discovery was tested on Fiber-shaped fixtures, through the real SDK.

36
00:02:34.995 --> 00:02:38.858
Follow-ups are rows, one per person, event and channel.

37
00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.262
In-app is always on.

38
00:02:40.262 --> 00:02:45.881
Email is opt-in, sent after the commit, claimed without duplicates, and retried.

39
00:02:45.881 --> 00:02:52.412
Delivery states are honest: a local test inbox is captured, a real mail server only accepted.

40
00:02:52.412 --> 00:02:59.505
The minute sweep enforces deadlines with bounded reminders, and resolution always needs the resident.

41
00:03:01.205 --> 00:03:08.803
A security review found one high and eight medium issues, all fixed or documented, with regression tests.

42
00:03:08.803 --> 00:03:13.507
TraceRoot spans cover intake, transitions, agent runs, discovery,

43
00:03:13.507 --> 00:03:17.342
email and the sweep, with only ids, enums and counts.

44
00:03:17.342 --> 00:03:22.480
Export was verified in version one; the new spans were not re-verified.

45
00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.834
The AI evaluation uses ninety-nine intake and fourteen coordinator cases,

46
00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.703
plus two held-out sets written independently.

47
00:03:31.703 --> 00:03:37.951
On held-out phrasing, the rules alone now miss six of thirteen hard emergencies, down from eleven.

48
00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:43.753
Run live, with the model reading the same words, the whole system escalated 11 of those 13.

49
00:03:43.753 --> 00:03:48.279
Live, the intake agent cut missed escalations from three in ten to one,

50
00:03:48.279 --> 00:03:55.037
and invented facts from five cases to one, but its false escalations rose from one to five of twenty-four.

51
00:03:55.037 --> 00:04:00.265
In both versions, policy blocked every forbidden action the coordinator attempted.

52
00:04:01.965 --> 00:04:10.792
Thirty-four unit tests, eighty-five API tests over HTTP and sixteen browser tests in real Chrome run in GitHub Actions on every push,

53
00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:15.570
against PostgreSQL and Mailpit, along with the evaluation's safety gate.

54
00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:21.135
And this is the actual GitHub Actions run for this release.

55
00:04:22.835 --> 00:04:28.006
What is not done: no live Fiber call, a small local model that over-escalates,

56
00:04:28.006 --> 00:04:34.370
rules that still miss indirect phrasing, and no real mail server, microphone test or deployment.

57
00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.955
Each is documented, with the next step.

58
00:04:38.655 --> 00:04:42.944
The model reasons, the backend decides, and people approve.

59
00:04:42.944 --> 00:04:47.670
The code, the tests, the evaluation and the limits are on GitHub.
